Z||000000||Turkey on Rye||11-24-2001||02:54 PM||||Is the balancer that i use on the right side of the engine right below the battery? I think my car needs to be timed pretty bad so if anyone can give me and hints or tricks on timing a fiero that woudl be awesome. Thank all of you very much.<BR>                      -Chris||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||11-24-2001||03:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Turkey on Rye:<BR><B>Is the balancer that i use on the right side of the engine right below the battery? I think my car needs to be timed pretty bad...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Sure, I'll help you time it pretty bad, if that's what it needs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.  Too bad you live on the "wrong"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> side of Kansas, or I'd bring my timing light over and help you out.  Only kidding about the "wrong" side of KS, of course.<P>The harmonic balancer is on the end of the crankshaft, RH side of the car, more or less right in line with the centerline of the engine.  It's way down there.  What you are probably looking at, below the battery, is the A/C compressor.<P>What engine do you have (4cyl or V6)?  If the underhood sticker is still intact, that will be a help...<P>||||reg||12
